@theme rivalry
// Writer-commons, themes batch. From content/arcs/outlines.md, "The struggle themes". Any department, either shift.
// Fill-ins assumed: {home} a place ("Lisk"), {family} with "my" ("my gran"), {hobby} an activity ("painting"),
// {since} a length of time ("five years"). A beat that names one lists it in needs:, so people without it skip it.
// Needs a rival bond ({rival}). Never cruel; the rival gets matching lines in their own file.

== beat 1
tone: light
when: bond:rival
hint: Oh, great. Look who it is. Not you. Over there. {rival}.
mem: sharp
them: Oh, look. {rival}'s here. Wonderful. Lovely. Marvellous.
them: Don't mind me. We have a history. A small one. It's grown.   [laugh]
? choice
* What happened?   flavour:listen mem:asked
  them: Long story. Short, actually. But it feels long. Another time.
* You two sound like an old double act.   flavour:cheer
  them: A double act? We'd never agree who was the funny one.   [laugh]
them: Anyway. We're very civil. Very, very civil.

== beat 2
tone: heartfelt
when: bond:rival
hint: You asked about {rival} once. Want the whole silly story?
mem: why
them: It started with a seat. In the mess. My seat. They sat in it. On my first day.   [sigh]
them: Then a joke at the wrong time. Then I said something back. Then it just kept going.
them: I don't even remember why it mattered. I just know it's been years of us being sharp.
? choice
* Sounds like it's been tiring.   flavour:listen mem:tiring
  them: It has. Being sharp all the time. It's very tiring.
  + them: It is. You're right. I'm tired of it. I don't think I'd noticed till now.
* Have you ever just said sorry?   flavour:practical mem:sorry
  them: Sorry? First? Me? ...Hm. No. No, I haven't.
them: A seat. Years over a seat. Don't laugh. Fine, laugh.

== beat 3
tone: resolution
when: bond:rival
hint: You'll never believe who I had tea with. Go on. Guess.
mem: madeup
them: I said sorry to {rival}. About the seat. About all of it.
them: And they laughed. They'd forgotten about the seat. They thought I'd been sharp about something else entirely.   [laugh]
them: We had tea. We're not friends yet. But we're not anything else either. It's nice.
? choice
* Proud of you.   flavour:cheer
  them: Don't. I'm being a better person. It's very uncomfortable.
  + them: Thanks. You put the idea in my head. I'll blame you if it goes wrong. It won't.
* Who gets the seat now?   flavour:cheer mem:seat
  them: We take turns. Very civil. Actually civil, this time.   [laugh]
them: Years. Over a seat. Honestly.
